{"name":"Blouson Blue","hex":"#67b7c6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blouson","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A garment drawn tight at the waist with blousing hanging over the waistband; a blouse jacket."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blouson"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blouson","blocks":[{"text":"A blouson or blouse jacket is a jacket that is drawn tight at the waist, causing it to blouse out and hang over the waistband. Originating in military uniforms of the mid-20th century, versions continue to be used as part of military, paramilitary and law enforcement uniforms in many places. As a piece of civilian clothing, it is considered to be both sportswear and casual clothing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Bundespolizei_blouson_gruen.jpg/330px-Bundespolizei_blouson_gruen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blouson","wikidata":"Q1760046"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/MA-1_Jacket_in_petrol.jpg/500px-MA-1_Jacket_in_petrol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/MA-1_Jacket_in_petrol.jpg/500px-MA-1_Jacket_in_petrol.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A modern nylon MA-1 flight jacket.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMA-1_Jacket_in_petrol.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/FBI-NYPD_Joint_Terrorist_Task_Force.jpg/330px-FBI-NYPD_Joint_Terrorist_Task_Force.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/FBI-NYPD_Joint_Terrorist_Task_Force.jpg/330px-FBI-NYPD_Joint_Terrorist_Task_Force.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"FBI-NYPD Joint Terrorist Task Force officers wearing raid jackets.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFBI-NYPD_Joint_Terrorist_Task_Force.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Jacket%2C_battledress_%28AM_1979.59-1%29.jpg/120px-Jacket%2C_battledress_%28AM_1979.59-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Jacket%2C_battledress_%28AM_1979.59-1%29.jpg/250px-Jacket%2C_battledress_%28AM_1979.59-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https:/